# Dark-Whisper - Project Memory

## Project Overview
**Dark-Whisper** (formerly Whisper Desktop) is a Windows dictation workspace (Electron). **Quick notes** (global hotkey) and **sessions** run whisper-stream live, append timestamped paragraphs to a Markdown file in a vault (quick notes: `Quick Notes/YYYY-MM-DD.md`, one per day), and refine each finished paragraph through the server. Transcription runs on a **bundled whisper.cpp server** by default; an external Whisper-compatible API (OpenAI or self-hosted) is also supported.

Repository: https://github.com/TheGeek01/Dark-Whisper (fork of dniasoff/whisper-desktop). Current version: 1.3.0.

### Key Features
- Global shortcuts: Quick Notes `Ctrl+Q` (refused while a session records and vice versa), Record `Ctrl+Alt+R` (session in the selected folder), Pause/Resume `Ctrl+Alt+P`, Stop `Ctrl+Alt+S`. Rules in `shared/shortcuts.ts`, registration in `shortcutRegistry.ts`; Settings fields capture keys and suspend the global shortcuts meanwhile
- Built-in whisper.cpp server, supervised by the app (start, health-check, restart, stop)
- Speech model manager: curated Hugging Face GGML models pinned by SHA256, plus custom model URLs
- GPU acceleration via Vulkan with automatic CPU fallback; "Force CPU" setting
- Tray icon with status tooltip, Show/Hide, Quick note, Models…, Exit
- Auto-start on Windows login
- Paragraphs close after `silenceGapSeconds` (5) of silence measured from the audio level, on Pause, on engine relaunch, or at `blockMinutes`; each starts with a `**HH:MM**` clock line and is refined unless edited; mic mute = pause
- Dark and light themes; frameless window (`titleBarOverlay`)

## Technical Stack
- **Framework**: Electron 44.4.0
- **Language**: TypeScript 6.0.3 (`module: node20`, CommonJS output)
- **Transcription**: whisper.cpp `b5130` (tag pinned in `whisper.version`), CPU + Vulkan builds
- **Audio**: node-mic 1.0.1 (bundles sox.exe; 16 kHz mono WAV)
- **HTTP**: axios 1.20.0 | **Settings**: electron-store 11.0.2 | **Multipart**: form-data 4.0.6
- **Build**: electron-builder 26.15.3 (config only in `electron-builder.yml`)
- **Tests**: Jest 30.5.1 + ts-jest | **Lint**: ESLint 10

## Architecture
Logic lives in Electron-free modules; one wiring module touches Electron. Jest cannot load Electron, so tests must never import `electron`, `electron-store`, `settingsService`, `whisperRuntime`, `streamRuntime`, `sessionRuntime`, `libraryRuntime`, `appIdentity` or `main`.

- **appIdentity.ts** — imported first by main: `app.setName('Dark-Whisper')` and the user-data migration
- **main.ts** — window (title bar overlay per theme), tray, global shortcuts, lifecycle, all IPC handlers
- **preload.ts** — `contextBridge` API; type-only imports so the bundle requires only `electron`
- **public/index.html** — workspace markup only (header, library, document, session panel), CSP-locked, loads `js/renderer/app.js`; `public/app.css` holds dark and light colour tokens and the CSS-mask icons

Electron-free services (unit-tested): `modelCatalog`, `modelManager`, `whisperServer`, `serverOutput`, `serverPaths`, `serverGate`, `settingsMigration`, `userDataMigration`, `streamOutput`, `streamEngine`, `sessionPaths`, `documentStore` (clock lines, `nextBlockIndex`, `setBlockRange`, `openOrCreate`), `guardedStore` (outside-edit detection, listeners), `guardRegistry` (one guard per document), `quickNotes`, `audioLevel` (`SilenceTracker`), `pcmFileSink`, `windowTheme`, `blockMath`, `sessionService`, `blockRefiner`, `micMuteOutput`, `micMuteService`, `libraryService` (vault tree, search, moves, path guard), `libraryWatch` (change batching, polling diff).
Electron-bound services: `whisperRuntime` (spawn, ports, `/health`, PID file, log file, stale cleanup), `streamRuntime` (whisper-stream spawn, session dirs, SoX raw PCM → WAV, per-recording audio entries and silence tracker, level events), `sessionRuntime` (sessions, outside-edit handling, refinement permission, mic mute), `settingsService`, `apiService`, `soxPath`, `libraryRuntime` (library IPC, `fs.watch` + 5 s polling fallback, Recycle Bin, open/reveal, vault picker).

## Workspace (stage 2)
- Renderer (`src/renderer/` → `public/js/`): vanilla TypeScript compiled by `tsconfig.renderer.json` (`npm run build:renderer`); `marked`/`DOMPurify` are copied to `public/vendor/` and used as classic-script globals (`src/renderer/globals.d.ts`). One state object (`state.ts`, `update(patch)`/`subscribe(listener)`) drives every pane's re-render.
- DOM-free, Jest-tested: `format.ts`, `libraryTree.ts`, `documentView.ts`, `sessionModel.ts`, `headerModel.ts`, `state.ts` — no `window`/`document`, ES2020 library features only (compiled through the tests by the main tsconfig too). DOM modules: `header.ts`, `library.ts`, `document.ts`, `levelMeter.ts`, `sessionPanel.ts`, `theme.ts`, `dialogs.ts`, `toast.ts`, `dom.ts`.
- `src/renderer/` and `src/shared/` (`api.ts`, types only) may import only each other; `.js`-extension imports, `import type` for types. The only `innerHTML` assignment is in `document.ts`, fed by `DOMPurify.sanitize`.
- CSP: `default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src data:; font-src 'none'; media-src 'none'; connect-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'` — no inline scripts or `style` attributes in `public/index.html`; images are `data:`-only (blocks remote/UNC image fetches from notes); links open in the OS browser, never in-app.
- Library IPC (`libraryService.ts`/`libraryRuntime.ts`): `library-tree`, `library-search`, `document-read`, `document-rename`, `document-move`, `document-delete`, `folder-create`, `document-open-external`, `document-reveal`, `choose-vault`, `copy-text`; `library-changed` (main → renderer, `{ paths }`, debounced 300 ms). All `file`/`folder` values are vault-relative with forward slashes (`''` = vault root) and go through a path guard; hidden entries (`.` prefix, e.g. `.obsidian`, `.trash`) are excluded.
- Watcher: `fs.watch` on the vault with a 5 s polling fallback (for network drives where `fs.watch` doesn't fire); changes are batched and diffed before `library-changed` fires.
- Delete moves files to the Recycle Bin (`shell.trashItem`), never a permanent delete.
- Recording-document lock: rename, move and delete of the document a session is currently writing are refused; `session-start` takes an optional target folder, and `session-status`/`session-block` (main → renderer) carry the per-block refinement state the session panel renders.
- `npm run smoke:workspace` (`scripts/workspace-smoke.mjs`) drives a real app instance over the DevTools protocol against a throwaway vault and a throwaway `--user-data-dir` profile, so it never touches the real settings or the installed app's single-instance lock. A hidden window with a title bar overlay renders no frames (dialog `close` never fires), so the script uses `--inspect` to `showInactive()` the window with only a corner on screen.

## Transcription API (same for built-in and external)
- `GET /health` (built-in) or `GET /v1/health` (external) — readiness
- `POST /v1/audio/transcriptions` — multipart `file`, returns `{ "text": ... }`
- Timeouts: built-in 300 000 ms, external 30 000 ms

## Server Lifecycle (whisperServer.ts)
States: `no-model` | `starting` | `ready` | `error` | `stopped`.
- Args: `-m <model file name> --host 127.0.0.1 --port <free port> --inference-path /v1/audio/transcriptions`, spawned with `cwd` = the model's directory. **The relative `-m` plus `cwd` is deliberate**: whisper-server reads argv as ANSI but decodes the path as UTF-8, so absolute paths break on non-ASCII profiles (e.g. `C:\Users\José`).
- Args add `--vad -vm <relative silero path>` when `refineVad` and the pinned model verifies; `vad-failed` (`failed to initialize VAD context`) relaunches without VAD. VAD loads per request in b5130.
- Readiness: poll `/health` every 500 ms up to 120 s (the model loads before the port opens).
- GPU label comes from the server log (`whisper_backend_init_gpu: using … backend` vs `no GPU found`), not from the chosen binary.
- Vulkan process exiting before readiness (without a model-load error) → retry on CPU and remember per version. Model-load failure → error, no fallback.
- Crash restarts: 1 s, 5 s, 15 s, then error; counter resets after 5 min healthy.
- Every launch bumps a generation counter; stale callbacks are ignored.
- PID written to `userData/whisper-server.pid`; a stale process is killed only if its image is `whisper-server.exe`.
- Binary resolution: `WHISPER_SERVER_DIR` (Vulkan, dev only) → `process.resourcesPath/whisper/<backend>/` when packaged → `<repo>/resources/whisper/<backend>/` in dev. Version read from `whisper/VERSION`.

## Live Sessions
- Engine: `whisper-stream.exe -m <live model> --step 0 --length 10000 -vth 0.6 -t <n> -l <lang> [-c <id>] [-ng] -f live.txt`, cwd `userData/sessions/<id>/`. Ready = stdout `[Start speaking]` (60 s). Diagnostics and the device list are on stderr; `streamOutput.ts` is the only parser of this format.
- Recording audio: SoX streams raw PCM (`-t raw -`) and `PcmFileSink` writes `audio-<n>.wav` (16 kHz 16-bit mono, 32 000 B/s, 44-byte header patched on close), never `--save-audio` (not real-time in VAD mode). SoX keeps running across engine restarts. SoX's `-S` level output is buffered until exit when piped, so levels are computed from the PCM.
- Blocks are paragraphs: `<!-- dw:block <n> t=<start>-<end> -->` then a clock line (`**HH:MM**`, date too for a recording's first); written lazily on the first words; closed on silence (SilenceTracker), Pause, relaunch, `blockMinutes` or Stop; closed non-empty block → RefineJob with SHA256 of its text (clock line excluded); replaced only if the text still matches. Quick notes: `Quick Notes/YYYY-MM-DD.md`, numbering continues after existing blocks, frontmatter duration accumulates, date fixed at start.
- Every read and write compares the file with what we last wrote (`GuardedStore`). An outside edit is accepted as the new baseline: edited finished blocks are skipped by their hash guard, the edited live block is marked and not queued, and all other blocks still refine. Each recording owns its queue and audio; recordings on the same file share one guard (`GuardRegistry`). Stop waits for SoX to exit before deleting session audio (Windows `EPERM` otherwise).
- Refinement allowed: built-in server ready (or external + `refineWithExternalApi`); during recording `auto` defers when live + refine model files > 2 GB. Audio deleted once the queue is empty unless `keepSessionAudio`.
- Mic mute shim: inline C# via powershell; needs `[ComImport]`, and 11 methods precede `SetMute` in `IAudioEndpointVolume`. Acts on the default capture device.
- Document name `<vault>/YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm-untitled.md`, `-2` on collision.

## Model Handling (modelCatalog.ts / modelManager.ts)
- Curated list pinned to size + SHA256; recommended model `ggml-large-v3-turbo-q5_0.bin` (547 MB).
- Custom URLs must match `https://huggingface.co/<owner>/<repo>/resolve/<rev>/<file>.bin`; id is `custom/<owner>__<repo>__<file>`; SHA256 read from `X-Linked-ETag` on Hugging Face's 302 (no-redirect HEAD first).
- Download to `<file>.part`, verify SHA256 + GGML magic (`readUInt32LE(0) === 0x67676d6c`), then rename. One download at a time; progress throttled to 250 ms; stray `.part` files swept at startup.

## Settings (electron-store, config.json)
`serverMode` (`builtin`/`external`), `modelId`, `forceCpu`, `gpuFallbackVersion`, `shortcut` / `recordShortcut` / `pauseShortcut` / `stopShortcut` (`""` = none), `apiUrl`, `apiToken`, `vaultPath`, `liveModelId`, `language`, `refineDuringRecording` (`auto`/`always`/`afterStop`), `refineWithExternalApi`, `refineVad` (default true), `blockMinutes`, `keepSessionAudio`, `silenceGapSeconds` (1–60, default 5), `theme` (`dark`/`light`), `captureDeviceName`.
Migration: if `serverMode` is absent and `config.json` already existed → `external` (upgrades keep working); fresh installs → `builtin`. `serverMode` is deliberately NOT in electron-store defaults, or the migration check would never fire.

## Data Locations (`%APPDATA%\Dark-Whisper\`)
`config.json`, `models\`, `logs\whisper-server.log`, `logs\stream.log`, `sessions\<id>\`, `whisper-server.pid`.
On first start `config.json`, `models`, `logs`, `recordings` move from `whisper-desktop` (then `Whisper Desktop`) unless the target already holds them.

## CI / Release
`.github/workflows/publish.yml` on a `v*.*.*` tag: lint → test (Ubuntu) → build-whisper (Windows: pinned Vulkan SDK 1.4.357.0 and SDL2, compiles CPU + Vulkan `whisper-server` and `whisper-stream` from `whisper.version`, smoke-tests a real transcription, caches per version) → build-and-release (downloads the artifact to `resources/whisper/`, builds NSIS, publishes a Release).

## Development Notes
- Re-check `serverOutput.classifyServerLine` and `streamOutput.ts` strings when bumping `whisper.version`.
- npm 12 skips dependency install scripts: after `npm ci`, restore SoX with `node scripts/postinstall.js` inside `node_modules/node-mic`.
- Electron 44 clipboard calls are async — always await them.
- The window uses `titleBarOverlay`: while hidden it renders no frames, so automated checks must show it (see the smoke script).
- In Git Bash, prefix manual server commands with `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1`, or `/v1/...` args get rewritten into Windows paths.
- Vulkan builds only come from CI; locally use `npm run whisper:fetch` (CPU) or `WHISPER_SERVER_DIR`.
- Tests use real temp directories and injected fakes; no real processes or network, so they pass on Ubuntu CI.
- Design spec and implementation plan: `docs/superpowers/`.
